-- title:
--   The $n$-th derived subgroup of $N$ consists of single-coordinate fractions when there are at most $n+2$ coordinates
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a group and $N$ a normal subgroup of $G$. Define the derived series of $N$ by $N^{(0)}=N$ and $N^{(n+1)}=[N^{(n)},N^{(n)}]$, the subgroup generated by the commutators $[a,b]=aba^{-1}b^{-1}$ with $a,b\in N^{(n)}$.
--
--   For an index set $\iota$, regard $G^\iota$ as a group under coordinatewise multiplication, write $e_i(g)$ for the tuple with $g$ in coordinate $i$ and $1$ elsewhere, and let $M\subseteq G^\iota$ be a submonoid. A tuple $z$ is a *right fraction* of $M$ if $z=uv^{-1}$ with $u,v\in M$. Consider the conditions:
--
--   1. (diagonal) every constant tuple $(g,g,\dots)$, $g\in G$, lies in $M$;
--   2. (pair inverse) for all distinct $i,j$ and every $v\in M$ there is $b\in M$ with $v_ib_i=1=v_jb_j$;
--   3. (pair coverage by $N$) for all distinct $i,j$ and all $a,b\in N$ there is $z\in M$ with $z_i=a$ and $z_j=b$.
--
--   Under condition 1, for each $i\in\iota$ the set $F_i(M)=\{g\in G: e_i(g)\text{ is a right fraction of }M\}$ is a (normal) subgroup of $G$.
--
--   **Theorem.** Let $n\in\mathbb N$. For every finite index set $\iota$ with $|\iota|\le n+2$ and every submonoid $M\subseteq G^\iota$ satisfying conditions 1–3, and for every $i\in\iota$,
--   $$N^{(n)}\subseteq F_i(M).$$
--
--   Thus pair coverage, which only controls two coordinates at a time, already yields single-coordinate fractions with an arbitrary element of $N^{(n)}$ in one coordinate and $1$ in all others, once the number of coordinates is at most $n+2$. Each additional coordinate costs one step of the derived series. In the Ramsey direction of the classification the theorem is applied with $N$ the exponent-sum-zero subgroup of a free group whose letters are points of space, to show that coordinatewise corrections by elements of $N^{(|\iota|-2)}$ can be realized by words built from congruent copies.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $N^{(n)}$ is `Derived N n`, $F_i(M)$ is `singleFractions M hd i`, and conditions 1–3 are `HasDiagonal M`, `PairInverse M`, `PairCoverage M N`. The index set is a `Fintype` with decidable equality and $|\iota|$ is `Fintype.card ι`; the statement quantifies over all such $\iota$ in one universe.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Combinatorics/EuclideanRamsey/DerivedFractions.lean#L124-L177

